00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:12.580
February 29th, 2020.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:18.520
The day of the first Coronavirus death in
the United States, reported at the time.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.869
The day, for Americans, that this mysterious,
highly-infectious disease went from distant

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:28.160
news story to actual, alarming reality.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.440
From the date of that first reported death,
it would take less than one month for the

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:38.120
U.S. to become the most infected country in
the world - passing Italy, then China, and

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.350
eventually ending up in a category of its
own.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:46.851
But although the outbreak was real everywhere,
it was felt viscerally in the northeast, one

00:00:46.851 --> 00:00:51.330
of only a handful of places in the country
where headlines of despair seemed to match

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.260
the daily experience of locals.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:01:00.610
There were not only two waves, but, effectively,
two, distinct, pandemics.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:06.650
For those in and around New York, the Coronavirus
was all-too-horrifyingly real, creating a

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:11.690
more vigilant atmosphere even now as new local
cases stabilize.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:18.640
Masks are widely worn, hands, frequently washed,
and public spaces, treated with caution.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.760
Outside of the northeast corridor, a very
different pandemic played out.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:30.130
One where the first casualties were jobs,
classes, and the conveniences of modern life.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:35.960
Reactions to government-imposed restrictions
were so geographically divided in part because

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.850
the Coronavirus was so geographically divided.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:45.110
Now, as infections surge across the country,
a once regional crisis is becoming a shared

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:46.400
disaster.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.190
Everyone, everywhere is, in some way, affected
by the virus.

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:56.390
But it would be a mistake to say that everyone
is affected equally.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:01.440
Just as in the early days of the pandemic,
there are, broadly speaking, two very different

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:07.540
groups of people: Those who’ve lost work,
school, and their livelihoods, and those who

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.899
can treat lockdown as a vacation.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:15.700
Generally speaking, this is an exceptionally
great time to be rich, and an exceptionally

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.420
bad time to be poor.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:23.390
Since March, around 50 million people have
filed for unemployment, setting records not

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.569
seen since the Great Depression.

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:30.650
Meanwhile, the country’s richest have seen
their wealth explode.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:36.120
During that same period, the net worth of
U.S. billionaires has grown by almost 20%,

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.530
and a dozen, in particular, have doubled their
wealth.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:44.930
When most Americans were stuck in their hometowns,
if not their living rooms, the richest among

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:50.670
us, now untethered geographically by work,
school, and friends, were on the move - to

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:55.240
their vacation homes in Jackson Hole, Nantucket,
and Sun Valley.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:00.720
There, in these small, remote towns, wealthy
families brought from their big cities the

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.510
risk of infection.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:08.200
Teton County, for example, of which Jackson
Hole is apart of, is one of the richest counties

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:13.770
in the country - home, at least during ski
season, of Bill Gates, Kanye West, Christy

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:17.180
Walton, and Dick Cheney, to name just a few.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:23.040
Its one and only hospital, equipped with just
24 ventilators, was put to the test as private

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.010
jets swarmed local airports.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:31.500
Despite being home to just 23,000 full-time
residents, Teton was Wyoming’s second-hardest-hit

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:37.950
county in April, surpassing other areas three
or four times more populous, until the second

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.480
wave hit.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:47.120
Other wealthy families booked-out entire hotels
or resorts for 20, 30, or $40,000 a week.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.180
Finally, some went even further - preferring
to leave the country altogether.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:58.540
Private jet companies were inundated with
requests, both from a lack of available scheduled

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.519
flights, and a concern for health and safety.

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:08.040
One study suggests regular passenger air travel
involves 270 person-to-person interactions,

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:12.010
while private flights expose a customer to
less than 20.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:17.359
But while demand for a safe place to hide
is clearly very high, it’s far harder to

00:04:17.359 --> 00:04:20.049
find supply.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:24.629
Pandemic tourists, as you might call them,
are looking for three things:

00:04:24.629 --> 00:04:29.880
Someplace Coronavirus is under control,
Somewhere that is isolated and likely to avoid

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.809
further outbreaks,
And, of course, somewhere that will let them

00:04:33.809 --> 00:04:34.990
in.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:40.629
The trouble is that any country which meets
the first two criteria likely did so by avoiding

00:04:40.629 --> 00:04:41.909
the third.

00:04:41.909 --> 00:04:47.319
In other words, any place where outbreaks
are contained likely closed its borders early,

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:50.539
and is unwilling to undo its hard work now.

00:04:50.539 --> 00:04:54.069
This rules out the vast majority of countries.

00:04:54.069 --> 00:04:59.569
Italy, for instance, denied entry to five
U.S. citizens who flew from Colorado earlier

00:04:59.569 --> 00:05:01.770
this month on a private jet.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:06.909
The risk of allowing them in, despite their
riches, is just too high.

00:05:06.909 --> 00:05:09.150
But not everywhere.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:14.210
There are a few countries where the benefits
of tourism are so, insanely high as to outweigh

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.860
the risk of further outbreaks.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:22.860
These are mostly small island nations like
Fiji, The Bahamas, and The Maldives.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:29.610
For the latter country, travel and tourism
comprise nearly 40% of its GDP.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.180
These are places that can’t afford to lose
visitors.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:38.150
But with limited healthcare infrastructure,
they really can’t afford an outbreak, and

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:42.610
therefore had to take the lesser of two very
bad evils.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.809
Take the case of Fiji.

00:05:44.809 --> 00:05:50.319
Its borders were first closed on February
3rd, weeks before the first confirmed case,

00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:55.159
to any foreigner who had visited mainland
China in the past 14 days, in addition to

00:05:55.159 --> 00:05:58.909
screening the health of passengers during
their flights to Fiji.

00:05:58.909 --> 00:06:04.699
On the 27th, this ban was extended to all
travelers from Italy, Iran, and parts of South

00:06:04.699 --> 00:06:05.699
Korea.

00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:12.849
18 days later, cruise ship stops, international
events, and government travel were also canceled.

00:06:12.849 --> 00:06:18.539
Three days after that, Fiji confirmed its
first case: a Fiji Airways flight attendant

00:06:18.539 --> 00:06:22.619
who had recently flown to San Francisco and
Auckland.

00:06:22.619 --> 00:06:28.490
After this first person began a chain community
transmission, infecting four others, locals

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.509
expected the worst.

00:06:30.509 --> 00:06:35.740
In early March, it became the first Pacific
island country to open a WHO-certified testing

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:41.009
lab, and the fourth Pacific country capable
of testing for COVID-19.

00:06:41.009 --> 00:06:46.770
This enabled instant results, rather than
waiting for samples to be sent to Australia.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:52.000
By the end of the month, its main international
airport was closed and a military-enforced

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.020
curfew announced from 10 pm to 5 am.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:02.430
Then, an amazing 78 days went by between its
eighteenth and nineteenth cases.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:10.310
As of early July 2020, despite a population
of 883,000 spread across 300 islands, Fiji

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:16.759
has recorded a total of 21 infections, making
it possible to list every past and present

00:07:16.759 --> 00:07:18.619
case in a single frame.

00:07:18.619 --> 00:07:25.030
It’s also managed a 100% recovery rate,
with the vast majority of recent cases coming

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:28.550
from returning locals staying in quarantine.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.969
In this way, Fiji perfectly encapsulates the
dilemma of countries like it: Having made

00:07:33.969 --> 00:07:39.839
early and painful sacrifices to prevent an
outbreak, they now have a new kind of vacation

00:07:39.839 --> 00:07:46.129
amenity: being free of Coronavirus, that they’re
eager to reap the benefits from, but at the

00:07:46.129 --> 00:07:49.909
risk of making things much, much worse.

00:07:49.909 --> 00:07:55.619
Every country, island, and city depends on
tourism to a different degree, and thus, every

00:07:55.619 --> 00:07:58.719
country, island, and city has responded differently:

00:07:58.719 --> 00:08:03.999
Cuba, for example, has divided the country
such that visitors stay only in designated

00:08:03.999 --> 00:08:07.789
resort areas and don’t infect the general
population.

00:08:07.789 --> 00:08:13.429
Hawaii, on the other hand, will allow travelers
to skip its mandatory two-week quarantine

00:08:13.429 --> 00:08:18.300
if they present a negative test result 72
hours before arrival.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:23.110
Fiji, like several other countries, has come
to a different conclusion:

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:27.539
It knows that the risk of welcoming visitors
is directly proportional to the number who

00:08:27.539 --> 00:08:33.349
arrive, but the number of visitors is not
necessarily proportional to the benefits they

00:08:33.349 --> 00:08:34.460
bring.

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:40.690
They can minimize the risk of reopening while
maximizing the income they generate by inviting

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:42.830
only the rich.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:48.310
To quantify this fact, Australia is the largest
source of arrivals in Fiji, accounting for

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:50.720
just under half of the total.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:58.720
They spend, on average, $116 US Dollars per
person, per day and $1,039 per trip.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:05.650
A cruise ship passenger, in comparison, spends
$44 on average per port of call.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:13.260
And finally, someone arriving by yacht spends
$3,615 during their average stay.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:18.410
In total, the yachting industry contributes
approximately 28 million dollars to the Fijian

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:25.660
economy every year, not that far behind the
44 million brought by the cruise industry.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:32.290
Cruise ships expose the islands to 239,000
passengers a year, while yachts expose them

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:35.930
to just 4,473.

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:41.550
By comparing these numbers, we can very crudely
estimate that yachts bring approximately 2%

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:47.110
the risk of infection that cruise ships do,
while contributing 63% as much to the local

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.330
economy.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:53.580
This is the thinking behind Fiji’s new ‘Blue
Lanes’ program, which allows billionaires

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:57.260
to bypass its Coronavirus border restrictions.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:01.330
Its prime minister announced that yachts and
pleasure craft will now be allowed to enter

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.060
one of its ports.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:08.090
If a ship’s journey there took 14 days or
longer at sea and its passengers show proof

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:13.360
of a negative test result, everyone on board
will be screened for symptoms, and, if deemed

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:16.400
healthy enough, allowed to roam the country.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:21.040
If their journey was shorter, they can make
up the remaining time in quarantine.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:26.130
If someone arrives from Sydney after 8 days
at sea, for example, they can pay for six

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:31.320
days of quarantine, and then proceed to hide
out on a remote private island.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:36.930
And Fiji is not alone, many countries are
competing for the VIP-crowd.

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:42.100
Seychelles is also allowing visitors who arrive
on private or chartered flights and then stay

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.840
on an isolated island resort.

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:49.660
Thailand, the Maldives, and other countries
have similar plans.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:55.110
In all likelihood, only a very small number
of billionaires will arrive - so far Fiji

00:10:55.110 --> 00:11:02.300
has announced 30, but that, is precisely the
goal - to cash-in on their strong early pandemic

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:06.940
response, while inviting very little additional
danger.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:12.470
If it works, international travel may slowly
revert to the status it once held decades

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:19.400
ago: reserved mostly for the rich, and fairly
inaccessible to everyone else.

